.TH ANUBIS 1 2026-10-01 "anubis 1.27.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
anubis \- proof-of-work HTTP proxy that challenges scraper bots
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B anubis
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B anubis
is a reverse proxy. It weighs each request against a policy and either
forwards it to the target, denies it, or answers with a challenge page
whose JavaScript proof of work a browser solves once; the browser then
holds a signed cookie and is forwarded.
.PP
Every option can also be set in the environment by its name in upper case
with dashes as underscores, for example
.B BIND
for
.BR \-bind .
The systemd unit
.B anubis@NAME.service
reads them from
.IR /etc/anubis/NAME.env .
.SH OPTIONS
The most used options follow;
.B anubis \-help
lists all of them with their defaults.
.TP
.BI \-bind " address"
Address to listen on (default :8923). Keep it on the loopback, behind the
web server.
.TP
.BI \-bind\-network " tcp|unix"
Address family of
.BR \-bind .
.TP
.BI \-metrics\-bind " address"
Address of the metrics and /healthz endpoint (default :9090).
.TP
.BI \-target " url"
Where allowed requests go: http://host:port or unix:///path.
.TP
.BI \-policy\-fname " file"
The policy (YAML or JSON); without it the built-in default applies.
.TP
.BI \-ed25519\-private\-key\-hex\-file " file"
File holding the hex-encoded 32-byte ed25519 seed that signs the cookies.
Without a key, a random one is generated at each start.
.TP
.BI \-difficulty " n"
Default challenge difficulty.
.TP
.B \-serve\-robots\-txt
Serve a robots.txt that disallows every robot.
.TP
.B \-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/anubis/NAME.env
Environment of the instance NAME.
.TP
.I /etc/anubis/NAME.key
Signing key of the instance NAME, readable by root only; the unit copies
it for the service at each start.
.TP
.I /etc/anubis/botPolicies.yaml
The default policy.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR anubis\-robots2policy (1),
.I /usr/share/doc/anubis/README.Debian
